`type`"},"2880":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-173","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#breaking-changes","content":"Low: two values are renamed"},"2881":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-174","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#breaking-changes","content":"Adapt consumers"},"2882":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-175","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#breaking-changes","content":"Independent re-enrollment authentication"},"2883":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-176","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#breaking-changes","content":"Any DMS"},"2884":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-177","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#breaking-changes","content":"Low: informational"},"2885":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-178","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#breaking-changes","content":"Read both blocks before editing"},"2886":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-179","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#release-scoped-resource-names","content":"Kubernetes derives a StatefulSet's PVC name from its pod name (`<volumeClaimTemplate>-<pod-name>`). Renaming the `kms` and `va` StatefulSets means `helm upgrade` binds brand-new, empty PVCs instead of the existing ones. The KMS key material and VA CRLs are not deleted — the old PVCs are orphaned, not removed — but the upgraded pods fail with `no such file or directory` (KMS) or `code=NotFound` (VA) until you copy the data across. This affects KMS when `services.kms.cryptoEngines` uses a `filesystem` engine and VA when `services.va.fileStore.type` is `local`. Every other renamed resource is stateless and is recreated without data-loss risk."},"2887":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-180","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#release-scoped-resource-names","content":"Step 4 of the migration guide copies the data."},"2888":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-181","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#strict-values-validation","content":"`values.schema.json` rejects unknown keys, so every block that 4.0.0 removed or renamed — `toolbox`, `auth.oidc.apiGateway`, `auth.authorization` and others — fails `helm lint` and `helm upgrade` outright. Step 2 lists every change."},"2889":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-182","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#credentials-in-kubernetes-secrets","content":"In 4.0.0 the chart reads PostgreSQL, AMQP and SMTP credentials from Kubernetes Secrets in the release namespace instead of inline values: `postgres.existingSecret`, `amqp.existingSecret` and — when SMTP authentication is configured — `services.alerts.smtp_server.existingSecret`, each with `usernameKey` and `passwordKey` naming the Secret data keys. The inline `postgres.username`/`postgres.password` and `amqp.username`/`amqp.password` values are removed and rejected by `values.schema.json`, so a 3.8.0 values file fails `helm lint` and `helm upgrade` until the credentials move into Secrets."},"2890":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-183","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#credentials-in-kubernetes-secrets","content":"The Secrets must exist before `helm upgrade` runs: the pre-upgrade database job connects to PostgreSQL with them. Step 2 creates them through the External Secrets Operator."},"2891":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-184","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#required-authorization-configuration","content":"3.8.0 had no authorization service, so a 3.8.0 values file has nothing to migrate from: you must add the `services.authz` configuration yourself. It needs the JWKS endpoint of your identity provider, the database mappings the authorization engine uses, and a bootstrap principal that matches how your provider assigns the administrator role. Without a matching principal nobody can administer the PKI."},"2892":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-185","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#gateway-token-validation-removed","content":"`auth.oidc.apiGateway.jwks`, `auth.authorization.rolesClaim` and `auth.authorization.roles.admin` are removed with no compatibility aliases, and the schema rejects them. Their settings move into `services.authz`: the JWKS URL becomes `services.authz.jwkUrl`, and the role claim and administrator role become a claim rule of the bootstrap principal. `auth.oidc.frontend` is unchanged."},"2893":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-186","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#non-root-containers","content":"Service images run on a distroless base as the numeric user `65532`; the `authz` image is Ubuntu with a non-root user that has the same UID. The per-service overrides `services.kms.securityContext.runAsGroup: 0` and `services.authz.securityContext.runAsUser`/`runAsGroup: 999` are removed; group access to the KMS volume and PKCS#11 socket is now handled by the pod-level `fsGroup: 65532`."},"2894":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-187","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#non-root-containers","content":"3.8.0 did not pin a container identity, so existing files can carry any UID. Any volume that holds keys or CRLs must be owned by `65532:65532`, or at least readable (and, where needed, writable) by that identity."},"2895":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-188","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#non-root-containers","content":"Pods now carry a pod-level `fsGroup: 65532` with `fsGroupChangePolicy: OnRootMismatch`, which skips recursive ownership changes when the volume root already has the expected group. If your backup helpers or jobs run with a different GID, verify they can still access the volumes they need."},"2896":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-189","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#amqp-over-tls","content":"In 3.8.0 `amqp.tls` was not applied and event-bus clients always connected over plaintext. In 4.0.0 `amqp.tls: true` switches them to AMQPS. The default `amqp.port` stays `5672` and does not change when TLS is enabled, so a values file that already set `amqp.tls: true` must point `amqp.port` at the broker's TLS listener (`amqps`, commonly `5671`), or set `amqp.tls: false` to keep plaintext. Clients must also trust the broker's certificate."},"2897":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-190","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#renamed-and-reshaped-values","content":"`toolbox` is renamed to `connectivityTest`, and the `helm test` hook uses the upstream `curlimages/curl` image pinned by digest."},"2898":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-191","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#renamed-and-reshaped-values","content":"`services.connectors` is a map keyed by connector ID instead of a list."},"2899":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-192","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#renamed-and-reshaped-values","content":"The `services.ui.port` default is `8085`, the unprivileged port of the rootless image."},"2900":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-193","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#renamed-and-reshaped-values","content":"The shared `probes:` block is replaced by independent `livenessProbe`, `readinessProbe` and `startupProbe` blocks."},"2901":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-194","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#renamed-and-reshaped-values","content":"With `tls.certManagerOptions.issuer` empty, the chart creates a release-scoped self-signed issuer, for example `lamassu-downstream-ca-selfsigned-issuer`. The legacy literal `downstream-ca-selfsigned-issuer` is still accepted and resolves to it."},"2902":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-195","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#renamed-and-reshaped-values","content":"Anti-affinity and topology spread must be configured explicitly through `affinity` and `topologySpreadConstraints`."},"2903":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-196","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#postgresql-consolidation","content":"Every 3.8.0 per-service database must end up as a schema of `pki`, keeping its structure, indexes, constraints, data and migration history. The Helm chart does this automatically; deployments without Helm do it by hand (see Deployments without Helm)."},"2904":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-197","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#postgresql-consolidation","content":"Two schema migrations abort on data that 3.8.0 allowed, so clean the data before upgrading:"},"2905":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-198","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#postgresql-consolidation","content":"The CA migration adds a UNIQUE constraint on `ca_certificates.id` and aborts if duplicate CA IDs exist. Imports already reject duplicates with `409`, so new ones cannot normally appear."},"2906":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-199","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#postgresql-consolidation","content":"The KMS migration promotes the primary key to `(key_id, engine_id)` and aborts with `cannot promote (key_id, engine_id) to primary key: N row(s) have no engine_id; backfill them before migrating` when `kms_keys` rows lack `engine_id`. Backfill `engine_id` first."},"2907":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-200","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#postgresql-consolidation","content":"The same KMS migration deletes, with a `NOTICE`, aliases that equal an existing key ID, because identifiers now resolve as a key ID before an alias. Affected aliases are dropped, not redirected."},"2908":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-201","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#sqlite-storage-removed","content":"The SQLite storage engine is removed, and the `couch_db` and `dynamo_db` engines are not registered in 4.0.0: their configuration constants remain, but they select no engine. Deployments on any of them must move to PostgreSQL and consolidate their data into the `pki` schemas before upgrading."},"2909":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-202","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#legacy-ca-keys-in-the-kms","content":"CA certificates of type `MANAGED` or `IMPORTED_WITH_KEY` whose private keys predate the KMS service have the key stored only in the crypto engine, under the certificate's `subject_key_id`, with no KMS record. The `ca-to-kms-migration` tool registers them:"},"2910":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-203","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#legacy-ca-keys-in-the-kms","content":"The `key_id` is the certificate's `subject_key_id`; it matches the SHA-256 digest of the public key only when the SKI was computed that way."},"2911":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-204","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#legacy-ca-keys-in-the-kms","content":"The tool is idempotent: keys already in the KMS are skipped, so it can be run several times."},"2912":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-205","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#legacy-ca-keys-in-the-kms","content":"Certificates that cannot be read, or lack an engine or a subject key ID, are skipped with a warning. Review the logs and resolve the affected records."},"2913":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-206","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#legacy-ca-keys-in-the-kms","content":"When CA certificates sharing a `subject_key_id` declare conflicting `engine_id`s, the tool fails that key and exits with code `1`, which fails a Helm pre-upgrade hook. Resolve the conflict manually before rerunning."},"2914":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-207","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#legacy-ca-keys-in-the-kms","content":"Once the keys are registered, certificates reference them in the database and the KMS refuses to delete a key that a certificate still uses (`409` `key is in use`). Deleting a certificate record removes it from the CRL and OCSP, so read Before deleting a key before freeing a key."},"2915":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-208","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#legacy-ca-keys-in-the-kms","content":"Optionally, installations with imported CAs from before 3.7 can start the KMS once with `crypto_engines.migrate_keys_format: true`: the KMS renames those SKI-named legacy keys to the SHA-256 digest of their public key (the old name is kept as an alias, and the certificate references follow automatically). Run it once and disable the option again; running it again is safe."},"2916":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-209","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#legacy-ca-keys-in-the-kms","content":"With Helm, enable the hook for the upgrade in step 2; without Helm, run the tool by hand."},"2917":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-210","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#references-between-certificates-keys-and-crl-settings","content":"Certificates now reference their KMS key, and CRL settings reference their signer certificate, so a key or certificate in use cannot be deleted. The KMS migration drops the legacy `lamassu.io/kms/binded-resources` key metadata. Before 4.0.0, deleting a CA could remove its key while leaving key references in its retained certificate records. The CA migration registers those missing keys in the KMS with only their public key to satisfy the retained references. These entries cannot be deleted while the retained certificates reference them; they do not restore the private key. In 4.0.0, deleting a CA releases the references from its own current certificate and linked reissued certificates before attempting to delete the key; other certificates that still reference it prevent deletion."},"2918":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-211","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"Stored webhook configs are rewritten to the current layout and their fields renamed:"},"2919":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-212","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"Field in 3.8.0"},"2920":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-213","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"Field in 4.0.0"},"2921":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-214","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`validate_server_cert`"},"2922":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-215","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`insecure_skip_verify` (value negated)"},"2923":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-216","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`oidc`"},"2924":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-217","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`jwt_options`"},"2925":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-218","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`apikey`"},"2926":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-219","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`apikey_options`"},"2927":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-220","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`mtls`"},"2928":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-221","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"`mtls_options`"},"2929":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-222","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"When the legacy mTLS certificate and key are both PEM, they move into `mtls_options.cert_content` and `mtls_options.key_content` and need no action. Two cases do need it."},"2930":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-223","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"**Webhooks with file references.** A mixed config, with a PEM certificate and a file-path key, is migrated to `mtls_options.cert_file` and `mtls_options.key_file`. Webhook delivery rejects those fields on every call, whatever the configured authentication mode, so every enroll and re-enroll that calls that webhook fails until the config is fixed. If the webhook uses mTLS, re-enter the certificate and key as Base64-encoded or plain PEM; if it does not, remove the leftover file fields. Metadata-only updates keep working in the meantime (`PUT` or `PATCH` on `/v1/dms/:id/metadata`). In a variant of the same problem, a stored config with file paths inside `mtls_options.cert_content` or `mtls_options.key_content` makes every full settings update (`POST /v1/dms` or `PUT /v1/dms/:id`) fail validation; settings are replaced wholesale, so resend the config with the certificate and key as PEM."},"2931":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-224","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-webhooks","content":"**Receiver certificate verification.** A config with `validate_server_cert: false` becomes `insecure_skip_verify: true`, so receiver verification stays skipped until that field is set to `false`. Correct it on every migrated config: the webhook authorization channel carries the API key or bearer token, and skipping verification exposes those credentials to a network-positioned attacker. Keep `insecure_skip_verify: true` only when the receiver certificate is deliberately unverifiable."},"2932":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-225","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#re-enrollment-trust-set","content":"The flat field `reenrollment_settings.additional_validation_cas` moves into the nested field `reenrollment_settings.est_rfc7030_settings.client_certificate_settings.validation_cas`:"},"2933":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-226","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#re-enrollment-trust-set","content":"The effective trust set does not change, because the nested value was never consulted when validating re-enrollments. If the flat list was missing or null, it becomes an empty list."},"2934":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-227","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#re-enrollment-trust-set","content":"What changes is how API requests are handled. Bodies that still carry `additional_validation_cas` are accepted, but the value is silently dropped because unknown JSON fields are ignored, and GET responses no longer include it. An update body built from the old layout therefore empties `validation_cas` without any error. Always read the DMS before sending an edit and reuse the layout the API returns."},"2935":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-228","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#fail-closed-revocation-checks","content":"Enrollment and re-enrollment now verify the revocation of the presented certificates and fail closed when it cannot be verified. There is no migration: every pre-existing DMS has the new `allow_unverifiable_revocation` option at its default `false`, so a certificate that is not managed by Lamassu and carries no OCSP or CRL distribution points is rejected until the option is set to `true` in the affected block, independently for the enrollment and the re-enrollment block."},"2936":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-229","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#fail-closed-revocation-checks","content":"Certificates that do carry endpoints are still strictly checked: unreachable endpoints, stale or inconclusive answers reject the certificate even when `allow_unverifiable_revocation` is enabled, and certificates managed by Lamassu are unaffected because their stored status is used. A validation CA revoked in Lamassu also rejects the operation, without falling back to the remaining validation CAs. See the DMS guide and Revocation and checks."},"2937":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-230","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#independent-re-enrollment-authentication","content":"Re-enrollment authentication settings are now stored independently from initial authentication. Nothing needs migrating, but read both blocks before editing a DMS so that you do not modify one while believing you are editing the other. The console exposes independent editors for both blocks; the DMS guide describes their fields, and you can also edit them through the DMS API."},"2938":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-231","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#dms-update-api","content":"`PUT /v1/dms/:id` takes the DMS ID from the URL and validates the request body. An ID in the body is ignored, so update clients that relied on it."},"2939":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-232","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#certificate-type-values","content":"Stored certificate type values are renamed: `IMPORTED` becomes `IMPORTED_WITH_KEY` and `EXTERNAL` becomes `IMPORTED_WITHOUT_KEY`. `MANAGED` is unchanged. Adapt consumers that read or match on those values."},"2940":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-233","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#device-events","content":"The `events` field no longer appears in the device representation. Point consumers at the new endpoints:"},"2941":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-234","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#device-events","content":"`GET /v1/devices/:id/events` returns a device's events."},"2942":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-235","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#device-events","content":"`POST /v1/devices/:id/events` creates an event."},"2943":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-236","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#device-events","content":"When the request `Accept` header includes `text/event-stream`, the events endpoint streams over SSE with a keepalive every 15 seconds, and returns `501` when SSE is disabled in the deployment. Each Device Manager instance binds a durable AMQP queue named after its service ID, `device-manager-sse-<uuid>`. Queues from crashed or replaced instances linger until removed, so configure an expiration or cleanup policy on the broker."},"2944":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-237","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-signer-field","content":"`crl_options.subject_key_id_signer` is replaced by the required `crl_options.signer_serial_number`, the serial number of the existing certificate that signs the CRL. A new CA's initial value is the serial number of its current certificate. Requests that still carry `subject_key_id_signer` return an error. The authorization entity that holds these settings is also renamed; see CRL settings keyed by CA ID."},"2945":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-238","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"In 3.8.0 the VA keyed each CRL by the CA's SKI, and `GET`/`PUT /v1/roles/{ca-ski}` read and updated it. In 4.0.0 the CRL settings of a CA are keyed by its CA ID, and every CA has its own, even when two CAs share a key:"},"2946":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-239","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"Route"},"2947":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-240","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"Operation"},"2948":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-241","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"`GET /v1/crl-settings`"},"2949":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-242","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"Lists the CRL settings; filterable at least by `ca_id`, `status` and `legacy_ski`."},"2950":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-243","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"`GET /v1/crl-settings/{ca-id}`"},"2951":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-244","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"Reads the settings of a CA."},"2952":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-245","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"`PUT /v1/crl-settings/{ca-id}`"},"2953":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-246","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"Replaces `crl_options`."},"2954":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-247","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"`DELETE /v1/crl-settings/{ca-id}`"},"2955":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-248","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"Removes the archived settings of a CA."},"2956":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-249","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"The options keep their meaning and their defaults: 7 days of `validity`, 6 days and 23 hours of `refresh_interval`, and `regenerate_on_revoke` `true`. `status` (`ACTIVE`, `FINAL` or `ARCHIVED`), `legacy_ski` and `latest_crl` are read-only. A `PUT` validates the signer only when it changes, does not regenerate the CRL, and returns `409` when the settings are not `ACTIVE`."},"2957":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-250","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"The public endpoint `GET /crl/{id}` takes the CA ID — the form the CDPs of newly issued certificates use — and keeps resolving the SKI form of certificates issued before the upgrade. Certificates issued before the upgrade keep their `/crl/<ski>` distribution points; newly issued ones carry `/crl/<ca-id>`, and both resolve to the same settings. The VA scheduled CRL job requests a new list on its first run, and the new list includes both URLs in its *Issuing Distribution Point*. Until it succeeds, the old list has only the legacy `/crl/<ski>` IDP: verifiers that compare it with the CDP of newly issued certificates cannot validate those certificates. The default schedule can delay the first run by up to about an hour; failures can extend the window."},"2958":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-251","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"The migration that turns VA roles into CRL settings cannot be rolled back: its rollback does nothing. CRLs generated after the upgrade are stored under the CA ID, where 3.8.0 does not look for them, and the archived settings of CAs deleted before the upgrade have no signer to go back to. Returning to 3.8.0 requires restoring both the database and the CRL bucket — the object storage that holds the published lists — from the backups taken before the upgrade."},"2959":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-252","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"The migration aborts, and the upgrade fails, on five kinds of data:"},"2960":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-253","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"CA IDs containing `/`: they cannot be used in CRL URLs. Recreate those CAs with a different ID."},"2961":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-254","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"An SKI shared by more than one CA: the error names the SKIs and asks you to recreate all but one of them on a different key."},"2962":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-255","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"A VA role whose signer certificate has no key: point the role to a signer with a key, or fix the key reference of the certificate, before upgrading."},"2963":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-256","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"A CA whose ID equals the `legacy-<ski>` ID the migration reserves for the archived settings of another role whose CA was deleted: recreate that CA with a different ID."},"2964":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-257","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"A CA ID equal to the SKI of another VA role: their CRL URLs would be ambiguous."},"2965":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-258","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"The settings of a CA deleted before the upgrade are migrated as `ARCHIVED`, with a `legacy-<ski>` ID and no signer: their last CRL is still served, but never regenerated, and `PUT` returns `409`. There is no API way back to `ACTIVE`. The CRL guide describes the full behavior."},"2966":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-259","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#crl-settings-keyed-by-ca-id","content":"**Custom authorization policies.** The entity `va_role` is renamed to `crl_settings`, with `ca_id` as its primary key and `signer_serial_number` as its relation to certificates. Update policies referencing the old entity. The entity gains the `delete` atomic action, a `signer_key_id` relation to KMS keys, and the filterable columns `signer_engine_id` and `signer_key_id`; grant the new action to whoever may delete archived CRL settings. Replace the 3.8.0 signer filter `crl_subject_key_id_signer` (or `crl_signer_certificate_serial_number` if used by an intermediate version) with `signer_serial_number`. Replace SKI filter values with the corresponding certificate serial numbers; renaming the filter alone is insufficient."},"2967":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-260","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#renamed-va-events","content":"`va.role.update` becomes `va.crl-settings.update` and `va.role.crl.init` becomes `va.crl-settings.init`; `va.role.crl.create` keeps its name and its payload. Every subject changes from `crl/<ski>` to `crl/<ca-id>`, and the payload of the renamed events changes from the old VA role to the CRL settings of the CA, with `ca_id` instead of `ca_ski`. The alerts migration renames the event types of existing subscriptions automatically, but it does not rewrite their conditions — JSON Path, JSON Schema or JavaScript: review conditions that filter on the old payload or on the old `crl/<ski>` subject, including those for `va.role.crl.create`. Direct event-bus consumers and audit searches must adopt the new names and payload themselves."},"2968":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-261","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#ca-signature-endpoints-removed","content":"`POST /v1/cas/{id}/signature/sign` and `POST /v1/cas/{id}/signature/verify` no longer exist: the CA service no longer signs or verifies arbitrary data, so a CA's private key only signs certificates. The Go SDK's `CAService.SignatureSign` and `CAService.SignatureVerify` methods are removed too, and the `ca.sign.signature` event is no longer published, so alert subscriptions and event-bus consumers that rely on it never fire again — remove those subscriptions and point consumers elsewhere. Sign and verify arbitrary data with a KMS key instead, through `POST /api/kms/v1/keys/{id}/sign` and `POST /api/kms/v1/keys/{id}/verify` (the Go SDK's `KMSService.SignMessage` and `KMSService.VerifySignature`); the console equivalent is described in Sign and verify. A CA is also only accepted for signing when its validity window includes the current time, even if its stored status still reads `ACTIVE`."},"2969":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-262","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#ca-ids-are-always-assigned-by-the-backend","content":"Creating or importing a CA registers it under a backend-generated UUID. Any `id` sent in the request body is ignored, and the field is removed from the create and import bodies. Scripts that supplied their own IDs and addressed CAs by them must read the ID the backend returns instead."},"2970":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-263","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#ca-signature-endpoints-removed-1","content":"A CA key now signs only certificates. 3.8.0 let a client sign arbitrary data with a CA key through `POST /v1/cas/{id}/signature/sign` and check the result with `POST /v1/cas/{id}/signature/verify`. 4.0.0 removes both endpoints, the matching `SignatureSign` and `SignatureVerify` methods of the Go SDK `CAService`, and the `ca.sign.signature` event. An alert subscription on that event no longer fires: delete it or move it to another event."},"2971":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-264","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#ca-signature-endpoints-removed-1","content":"To sign and verify data, use the KMS operations `POST /v1/keys/{id}/sign` and `POST /v1/keys/{id}/verify`, which have their own authorization. Signing a certificate with a CA that is not `ACTIVE` or whose validity period does not include the current time now fails with `400`, even if the stored status has not yet changed to `EXPIRED`: see Certificate authorities."},"2972":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-265","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#va-crl-signer","content":"The VA migration resolves each role's signer from its stored SKI. It first looks for CA certificates with that SKI; if several match, it selects the oldest CA and logs a warning. If no CA certificate matches, it looks among all certificates with that SKI. The migration aborts with `cannot resolve signer certificate for VA role <ca-ski>, SKI <ski>` if that fallback finds zero or multiple candidates. Fix affected roles before upgrading."},"2973":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-266","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#helm-migration-guide","content":"The upgrade runs in a fixed order: prepare the data and values, run `helm upgrade`, then copy the KMS and VA data into the new volumes. The copy must run after the upgrade, because the destination StatefulSets and PVCs do not exist before it. If you are not upgrading an existing release, go straight to Install with Helm."},"2974":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-267","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-1-prepare","content":"Take a verifiable backup of PostgreSQL and of the CRL object storage — the VA bucket, or the local volume that holds the CRLs — and schedule downtime. The upgrade moves every service's data into `pki`, and the VA migration is irreversible: returning to 3.8.0 needs both backups (see CRL settings keyed by CA ID)."},"2975":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-268","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-1-prepare","content":"If the deployment runs on SQLite, `couch_db` or `dynamo_db`, move it to PostgreSQL first."},"2976":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-269","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-1-prepare","content":"Resolve duplicate CA IDs and backfill `engine_id` in `kms_keys`, as described in PostgreSQL consolidation."},"2977":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-270","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-1-prepare","content":"Optionally, run the pre-upgrade check against the consolidated 3.8.0 data before applying the migrations."},"2978":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-271","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-1-prepare","content":"Record the names of your local-storage PVCs:"},"2979":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-272","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-1-prepare","content":"`helm upgrade` does not touch or delete the old PVCs, but nothing references them after the upgrade. You need their names to copy the data and to clean up later."},"2980":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-273","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#pre-upgrade-check","content":"The 4.0.0 database migrations refuse data they cannot migrate safely: they abort and name the offending objects. The `upgrade-check` tool reports all of those problems before the upgrade, in one run, with the same wording the migration would use. It is read-only: it never writes database rows or keys."},"2981":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-274","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#pre-upgrade-check","content":"Image: `ghcr.io/lamassuiot/lamassu-upgrade-check`. Configure it with a KMS-style YAML file passed through `LAMASSU_CONFIG_FILE`; only the `postgres` storage provider is supported."},"2982":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-275","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#pre-upgrade-check","content":"Run it on the 3.8.0 data after it has been consolidated into the `pki` schemas, and before any 4.0.0 migration runs or any 4.0.0 service starts."},"2983":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-276","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#pre-upgrade-check","content":"Exit codes: `0` means no problems were found, `1` means at least one problem was found, and `2` means the command could not run (bad configuration, unreachable database, or a database that is not a 3.8.0 one), or a check could not run."},"2984":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-277","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#pre-upgrade-check","content":"It covers the VA migrations only: an all-clear does not prove that the CA and KMS migration guards pass, so it does not replace the duplicate CA ID and `engine_id` checks described in PostgreSQL consolidation."},"2985":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-278","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"**Create the credential Secrets.** The 4.0.0 chart reads PostgreSQL, AMQP and SMTP credentials from Kubernetes Secrets, and the pre-upgrade database job needs them before the upgrade runs. Copy the 3.8.0 credentials into your secret-management provider and create the Secrets with the External Secrets Operator (ESO), which the chart does not install:"},"2986":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-279","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"Configure ESO and its provider (`SecretStore` or `ClusterSecretStore`)."},"2987":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-280","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"Create an `ExternalSecret` for each credential set you use. Its target Secret must live in the release namespace, be named after the corresponding `existingSecret` value, and contain these keys:"},"2988":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-281","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"Secret (`existingSecret`)"},"2989":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-282","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"Required data keys"},"2990":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-283","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"When"},"2991":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-284","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"`lamassu-postgres` (default of `postgres.existingSecret`)"},"2992":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-285","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"`username`, `password`"},"2993":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-286","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"Always"},"2994":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-287","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"`lamassu-amqp` (default of `amqp.existingSecret`)"},"2995":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-288","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"`username`, `password`"},"2996":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-289","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"Always"},"2997":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-290","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"`services.alerts.smtp_server.existingSecret`"},"2998":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-291","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"`username`, `password`"},"2999":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-292","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"Only when SMTP authentication is enabled"},"3000":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-293","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"Wait for every `ExternalSecret` to be Ready and verify the generated Secrets before running the upgrade."},"3001":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-294","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"Do not change the database or broker passwords as part of this migration: ESO synchronizes credentials into Secrets, but it does not update the users configured on the PostgreSQL server or the broker. Removing credentials from the values file does not undo past exposure — if they were ever committed to Git, rotate them after the migration is complete."},"3002":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-295","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"The `charts/lamassu/README.md` in the Helm repository documents a full worked example in its *Secret management* section: installing external-secrets 0.20.2, a test Fake `ClusterSecretStore`, the `ExternalSecret` resources and the wait for synchronization. Its Fake provider is for testing only; for production, replace it with your provider's configuration."},"3003":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-296","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"**Add `services.authz`.** Configure the JWKS endpoint, the database mappings and the bootstrap principal:"},"3004":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-297","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"`jwkUrl` is fetched from the `authz` pod, not from the gateway, so a Service in the release namespace can be referenced by its short name. The default points at a Keycloak Service named `auth-keycloak`; set it explicitly if your identity provider lives anywhere else."},"3005":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-298","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"`authz` is the authorization service's own storage for principals, grants and policies. `pki` is the database the authorization engine queries when it evaluates policies against entities. Only the `database` field of each entry is required; per-schema `hostname` and `port` values remain accepted but are ignored — the connection always uses the global `postgres.hostname` and `postgres.port` with the global PostgreSQL credential Secret, `postgres.existingSecret` with its configured key names, unless the entry sets its own `existingSecret` (with optional `usernameKey` and `passwordKey`)."},"3006":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-299","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"If you kept the 3.8.0 role defaults (`realm_access.roles` and `pki-admin`), the default `services.authz.bootstrap` already matches them."},"3007":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-300","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"**Delete the gateway token validation blocks.** Remove `auth.oidc.apiGateway` and `auth.authorization` once their settings are in `services.authz`:"},"3008":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-301","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"**Rename `toolbox` to `connectivityTest`:**"},"3009":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-302","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"**Remove the per-service identity overrides** `services.kms.securityContext.runAsGroup` and `services.authz.securityContext.runAsUser`/`runAsGroup`."},"3010":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-303","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"**Convert `services.connectors` to a map** keyed by connector ID, each entry with its `type` and `image`:"},"3011":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-304","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"**Check AMQP.** If you set `amqp.tls: true`, also set `amqp.port` to the broker's TLS listener (commonly `5671`), or set `amqp.tls: false` to stay on plaintext."},"3012":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-305","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"**Enable the CA-to-KMS migration** if your CA keys predate the KMS:"},"3013":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-306","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"**Review the remaining values:** overrides that pinned `services.ui.port` to `80`, the old `probes:` block, the TLS issuer, and explicit `affinity` and `topologySpreadConstraints` where your cluster needs them. Renamed and reshaped values describes each one."},"3014":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-307","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-2-update-the-values-file","content":"Run `helm lint` with the new values before upgrading; the strict schema reports any key that is still unknown. Before running Step 3, confirm every credential `ExternalSecret` is Ready and the generated Secrets contain the expected keys."},"3015":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-308","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-3-run-the-upgrade","content":"Helm runs the pre-upgrade hooks — the CA-to-KMS migration when enabled, and the database job — before applying any workload, so services never start against an unprepared database. If validation rejects unknown values, fix the values file and re-run."},"3016":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-309","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-3-run-the-upgrade","content":"If the deployment uses local KMS or VA storage, those pods fail until you complete step 4, so `--wait` cannot succeed: Helm waits for them to become ready, times out, exits with an error and marks the release `failed`. The hooks have already run by then, and every manifest, including the new StatefulSets and their PVCs, has been applied. Helm does not roll anything back without `--atomic`. Continue with step 4, then re-run the same `helm upgrade` command so it completes and Helm records the release as `deployed`. Both hooks are idempotent, so they are safe to run again."},"3017":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-310","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"Skip this step when `services.kms.cryptoEngines` never used a `filesystem` engine and `services.va.fileStore.type` was never `local`."},"3018":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-311","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Find the new StatefulSets and PVCs.** Their names depend on the release name and any `nameOverride` or `fullnameOverride`; the PVC name is `<volumeClaimTemplate>-<StatefulSet name>-0`:"},"3019":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-312","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"With release `lamassu` and the default chart name, the new PVCs are `golang-engine-storage-lamassu-kms-0` and `local-crl-file-storage-lamassu-va-0`; with release `prod` they are `golang-engine-storage-prod-lamassu-kms-0` and `local-crl-file-storage-prod-lamassu-va-0`. Confirm both old and new PVCs exist before continuing. If `claims_ok` prints `ABORT`, the block stops before listing the claims: either a StatefulSet lookup failed, or a new claim resolves to the 3.8.0 claim. In the second case the copy would verify against itself and the final cleanup would delete the live volume. The chart always appends `-kms` and `-va` to the release-scoped name, so a collision means the claims are not what this guide expects; investigate before going on. Item 3 runs the same check and refuses to create the helper pod, so nothing touches the volumes. The check returns instead of calling `exit`, which would close your shell and lose the variables set so far. If you only migrate one of the two services, drop the other one's claims from the commands that follow."},"3020":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-313","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Record the replica counts, scale the new StatefulSets down and wait for every pod that uses the claims to exit**, so nothing writes to either volume while you copy. Helm removes the 3.8.0 `kms` and `va` StatefulSets during the upgrade, but their pods `kms-0` and `va-0` can still be terminating and holding the old claims. While they run, the helper pod either cannot attach the claims or copies a volume that is still being written. The `wait` returns at once for pods that are already gone:"},"3021":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-314","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Run a short-lived helper pod** that mounts all four claims. It runs as root so it can change file ownership, so pin its image by digest and do not mount the service-account token:"},"3022":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-315","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Inspect before writing** so you do not clobber data the new pods may already have written:"},"3023":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-316","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"An empty result is the common case: a StatefulSet's own pod rarely gets far enough to write anything when its dependent data is missing. If the output is not empty, record the files and confirm with the service owner that they are disposable before you run the copy; do not overlay the 3.8.0 data onto an unknown store."},"3024":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-317","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Copy the data, align ownership and verify the copy.** The second command must print `copy verified`; any `diff` output means the copy is incomplete, so do not continue:"},"3025":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-318","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"The `chown` is required even if the old files already look non-root-owned, because 4.0.0 requires exactly `65532:65532` and does not fall back to whatever the image declares."},"3026":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-319","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Remove the helper and restore the recorded replica counts:**"},"3027":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-320","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-4-migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Re-run the step 3 `helm upgrade` command.** The KMS and VA pods now start against the copied data, so `--wait` succeeds and the release moves from `failed` to `deployed`."},"3028":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-321","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-5-remove-the-one-off-migration-values","content":"After the upgrade that performed the CA-to-KMS migration succeeds, remove `migrations.caToKms.enabled` from your values (it defaults to `false`). The hook reads the legacy 3.8.0 `kms-config` ConfigMap while it still exists and falls back to the release-scoped `<release>-lamassu-kms-config` once it is gone."},"3029":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-322","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#step-5-remove-the-one-off-migration-values","content":"Then go through the validation checklist. Keep the old PVCs until it passes."},"3030":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-323","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#deployments-without-helm","content":"Without the chart's database job, no tool moves data between databases: the migration tooling only applies migrations to a schema that already exists. Move each per-service database into its `pki` schema yourself, preserving structure, indexes, constraints, data and migration history, with writes stopped and a verified backup in hand."},"3031":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-324","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#deployments-without-helm","content":"Run the migrations in the required order, one schema at a time: `kms` first, then the `ca-to-kms-migration` tool (needed only for legacy deployments whose CA keys are named by SKI), then `ca`, then `va`. The `devicemanager`, `dmsmanager` and `alerts` schemas are independent and can be migrated in any order. With Helm, the chart's pre-install job applies the schemas in the correct order automatically."},"3032":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-325","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#deployments-without-helm","content":"If `kms` has not been migrated, the `ca` migration fails with `kms schema not found: migrate the kms schema before the ca schema`. The `va` migration requires `ca` and `kms` to be migrated first: it fails with `ca schema not found: migrate the ca schema before the va schema` or `kms schema not found: migrate the kms schema before the va schema` if one of them is missing."},"3033":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-326","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#deployments-without-helm","content":"The schemas reference each other, so the PostgreSQL role running the migrations needs cross-schema privileges: the `ca` schema needs `USAGE` on `kms` plus `SELECT`, `REFERENCES` and `INSERT` on `kms.kms_keys`, and the `va` schema needs `USAGE` on `ca` plus `SELECT` and `REFERENCES` on `ca.certificates`, `SELECT` on `ca.ca_certificates`, and `USAGE` on `kms` plus `SELECT` and `REFERENCES` on `kms.kms_keys`. Without them the migration aborts; grant the missing privileges and rerun the failed schema. After migrating `ca`, if the CA service runs as a different user than the migration user, grant it `SELECT` on `ca.certificates_view` (`GRANT SELECT ON ca.certificates_view TO service_user`). Without this grant, certificate and CA reads fail with `permission denied for table certificates_view`. After migrating `va`, if the CA service runs as a different user, grant it `USAGE` on the `va` schema and `SELECT` on `va.crl_settings` (`GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA va TO service_user; GRANT SELECT ON va.crl_settings TO service_user`): the CA service reads `va.crl_settings` when it deletes a CA, and without these grants every deletion of a CA that has a crypto engine fails with `permission denied for schema va` (or `for table crl_settings`)."},"3034":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-327","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#deployments-without-helm","content":"To apply migrations by hand, `goose-lamassu` must run against the `pki` database with `search_path=<schema>` in the connection string. The binary validates only `search_path`, not the database name, so check `dbname=pki` before running it, and repeat for `kms`, `ca`, `va`, `devicemanager`, `dmsmanager` and `alerts`:"},"3035":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-328","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#deployments-without-helm","content":"Run `ca-to-kms-migration` first with `--dry-run`, which reports without writing to KMS storage, and then for real:"},"3036":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-329","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#deployments-without-helm","content":"Point the tool's `storage` configuration at the `pki` database, where the CA and KMS data now live in the `ca` and `kms` schemas. The tool's options are described in `backend/cmd/ca-to-kms-migration/README.md` in the `lamassuiot` repository."},"3037":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-330","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#deployments-without-helm","content":"Both tools' READMEs document the 4.0.0 `pki` layout and match this page: `goose-lamassu` uses `dbname=pki` examples and does not validate the database name, and the `ca-to-kms-migration` README describes the single `pki` database and the migration order."},"3038":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-331","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**KMS or VA pods crash with `no such file or directory` or `code=NotFound` right after the upgrade.** The pods are bound to the new, empty PVCs and the data migration has not run yet, or was copied into the wrong PVC. Follow step 4 and check that all four claims exist."},"3039":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-332","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**`helm upgrade --wait` times out and `helm status` reports the release as `failed`.** With local KMS or VA storage this is expected on the first run: the new pods cannot become ready before their data is copied. The hooks ran and the manifests and PVCs were applied, so complete step 4 and re-run the same `helm upgrade` command. If other pods are also not ready, check their logs, because something else is wrong."},"3040":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-333","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**The helper pod stays `Pending` or `ContainerCreating` and `kubectl wait` times out.** Another pod still holds one of the claims; on block storage `kubectl describe pod pvc-migrate-helper` shows a `Multi-Attach error`. Check with `kubectl get pods -n $NAMESPACE` that `kms-0`, `va-0` and the new KMS and VA pods are gone, then re-run the wait."},"3041":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-334","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**`helm upgrade` fails with an unknown-key validation error.** Remove or rename the legacy values — typically `toolbox`, `auth.oidc.apiGateway` or `auth.authorization` — because the strict schema rejects keys it does not know."},"3042":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-335","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**The upgrade fails at the database job.** The PostgreSQL role cannot create databases or schemas, or a schema migration aborted: on duplicate CA IDs or missing `engine_id` values, or in the VA schema on a CA ID containing `/`, an SKI shared by more than one CA (the error asks you to recreate all but one of them on a different key), a role whose signer certificate has no key, a CA ID reserved for the archived settings of another role, or a CA ID equal to another role's SKI. The abort message names the offending objects; fix them and re-run the upgrade."},"3043":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-336","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**The upgrade fails at the CA-to-KMS hook.** CA certificates that share a `subject_key_id` declare conflicting `engine_id`s. Resolve the conflict and re-run."},"3044":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-337","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**Nobody can log in after the upgrade.** Check that `services.authz.jwkUrl` is reachable from the `authz` pod, that `services.authz.bootstrap` matches a role your OIDC provider actually assigns, and that the database job completed."},"3045":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-338","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**A migration aborts with `kms schema not found`.** The schemas must be migrated in order: run the `kms` schema migration before the `ca` and `va` schema migrations."},"3046":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-339","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**A migration aborts with `ca schema not found`.** Run the `ca` schema migration before the `va` schema migration."},"3047":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-340","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**The VA migration fails with `cannot resolve signer certificate for VA role ... N candidates`.** The migration cannot uniquely identify a signer certificate from the SKI stored on the role. Review the SKI and candidate certificates reported in the error; correct the pre-migration data with a verified backup and rerun the migration. The new `signer_serial_number` field is created during that migration, so it cannot be set through the VA API while the migration is failing."},"3048":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-341","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#troubleshooting","content":"**A migration or service fails with `permission denied for table ...` or `permission denied for schema ...`.** The PostgreSQL role is missing the cross-schema privileges listed in Deployments without Helm; this includes `certificates_view` when the post-migration `GRANT SELECT` was skipped, and `permission denied for schema va` (or `for table crl_settings`) when deleting a CA without the `va` grants. Grant the missing privileges and re-run."},"3049":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-342","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"After the upgrade, check in this order:"},"3050":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-343","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Databases.** Each service reads the `pki` database with its own schema, `authz` and `wfx` data are reachable, and the migration status is registered per schema, including the CA unique-ID and KMS composite-key migrations and the foreign-key migrations that run per schema in the required order."},"3051":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-344","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**KMS and VA start cleanly.** Their logs show no `no such file or directory` or `code=NotFound` errors."},"3052":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-345","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Existing KMS keys work.** Issue a certificate from a CA that existed before the upgrade. None of the other checks reads a KMS key, so this is the only one that proves the key material was copied."},"3053":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-346","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Existing CRLs are served.** `GET /crl/<ca-id>` on VA returns a previously issued CRL, and `GET /crl/<ca-ski>` with the legacy SKI of a certificate issued before the upgrade also resolves. The VA scheduled CRL job has issued a new list under the CA ID with both URLs in its IDP; check its logs if regeneration has not succeeded."},"3054":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-347","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Renamed VA events.** Alert subscriptions to `va.role.update` and `va.role.crl.init` now subscribe to `va.crl-settings.update` and `va.crl-settings.init`, and conditions for all VA events, including `va.role.crl.create`, have been reviewed against the new payload (`ca_id` instead of `ca_ski`) and subject (`crl/<ca-id>` instead of `crl/<ski>`). Direct consumers and audit searches use the new event names."},"3055":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-348","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Legacy CA keys.** If the CA-to-KMS migration ran, review its report and warnings and confirm the expected keys appear in the KMS. Migrated CA certificates now report `key_id` and `has_private_key`, which you can use to confirm the registration."},"3056":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-349","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Connectivity.** `helm test \"$RELEASE\" -n $NAMESPACE --logs` passes; the hook checks the CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA health endpoints and the UI response."},"3057":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-350","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Authorization.** Sign in as the bootstrap principal and confirm administration works, check that an identity without permissions receives `403`, and review client and integration permissions."},"3058":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-351","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**AMQP.** The backend connects to the broker with the expected TLS settings, and the cleanup policy for SSE queues is in place."},"3059":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-352","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Device events.** `GET /v1/devices/:id/events` returns the historical events of a device that had them."},"3060":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-353","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Webhooks without file fields.** For each DMS that uses a webhook for enrollment or re-enrollment, the `config` block carries `insecure_skip_verify` and the expected option block (`apikey_options`, `jwt_options` or `mtls_options`), with the certificate and key as PEM and no `cert_file` or `key_file`."},"3061":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-354","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Receiver verification.** `insecure_skip_verify` is `false`, unless the receiver certificate is intentionally unverified."},"3062":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-355","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Webhook delivery.** One enroll or re-enroll through each migrated webhook completes its authorization call."},"3063":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-356","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**Trust set.** `est_rfc7030_settings.client_certificate_settings.validation_cas` holds the expected CAs, in particular those of the old CA during rotation overlaps."},"3064":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-357","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#validation-checklist","content":"**API clients.** Scripts and consoles no longer use the old DMS layout (flat `additional_validation_cas`, or the legacy `mtls`, `apikey` and `oidc` fields), send DMS updates with the ID in the URL, and match on the new certificate `type` values."},"3065":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-358","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#delete-the-old-volumes","content":"Only once every check passes, delete the orphaned 3.8.0 volumes to reclaim storage. The delete is irreversible and the old KMS volume may hold the last copy of your CA key material, so take a `VolumeSnapshot` or a backup of both old PVCs first and keep it until you are confident the upgraded deployment is healthy. These are the fixed 3.8.0 names recorded in step 1; before deleting, confirm that neither is mounted by a running pod, for example with `kubectl describe pvc -n $NAMESPACE golang-engine-storage-kms-0 local-crl-file-storage-va-0`, where `Used By` must be `<none>`:"},"3066":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-359","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#delete-the-old-volumes","content":"The 3.8.0 per-service databases are no longer used either. Drop them only after the same checks pass and your PostgreSQL backup is verified."},"3067":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-360","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#delete-the-old-volumes","content":"<Card title=\"Install with Helm\" description=\"Prepare dependencies, configure values and install a controlled deployment.\" href=\"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm\" />"},"3068":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-361","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#delete-the-old-volumes","content":"<Card title=\"Access control\" description=\"Principals, policies and the first administrator.\" href=\"/docs/platform/administration/access-control\" />"},"3069":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0-362","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-83/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0#delete-the-old-volumes","content":"<C