ew dependencies and any provider resources already created if an operation fails partway through."],[26,"After deployment"],[1976,"After the deletion, the settings are archived and the last CRL keeps being served but is never regenerated; you can remove them once no certificate issued by the CA still needs revocation evidence, using `DELETE /v1/crl-settings/{ca-id}` or the console's **Verification Authorities** page. Deleting them stops the CRL from being served and cannot be undone. Adjust the validity and signer before revoking or deleting the CA (see CRL). The CA’s key is released, but the KMS keeps it while other certificates still reference it."],[3028,"After the upgrade that performed the CA-to-KMS migration succeeds, remove `migrations.caToKms.enabled` from your values (it defaults to `false`). The hook reads the legacy 3.8.0 `kms-config` ConfigMap while it still exists and falls back to the release-scoped `<release>-lamassu-kms-config` once it is gone."],[3049,"After the upgrade, check in this order:"],[478,"after updating the CA or client certificate Secret, restart the consuming pods: the AMQP client loads certificates at startup."],[812,"alert if it stops consuming or the pending queue grows."],[473,"alert on orphan durable queues and backlog growth."],[2847,"Alert subscriptions and consumers of the VA events"],[709,"Alerts and subscriptions"],[2029,"Align the duration with the fleet's real renewal capacity. Leave margin against the CA's expiration."],[1059,"All ancestors are not added automatically. Trust distribution distinguishes trusted roots, intermediates and initial server trust."],[323,"All Gateways can use 80/443; requires a load balancer with an address pool"],[311,"Allocate a VIP from an address pool reachable on your LAN. You may request that VIP with `gateway.addresses` if the selected implementation supports it. Confirm the assigned address in status rather than assuming the request succeeded."],[2010,"allow or block ECDSA keys;"],[2008,"all