lls the stored target, and saving rewrites the channel configuration in the current layout."],[722,"Subscriptions turn Lamassu events into actionable notifications. You can alert a team, feed an incident system or trigger an automation when a CA, certificate or device changes."],[793,"Successful operations use a type prefixed with audit.. Failures publish the operation type suffixed with .error. The CloudEvents event additionally adds source, identifier, date and type."],[61,"Support"],[2684,"Supported versions"],[1843,"Switch issuance"],[1325,"Switch issuance, renew in cohorts and compare the installed serial with the active slot. Remove previous trust once no legitimate equipment needs it and policy permits ending overlap. Follow Hierarchy and rotation for the PKI operation."],[835,"Switch to the low level to see the internals of the Lamassu platform box (CA, KMS, DMS, Device Manager, VA, Alerts, AWS IoT connector, Job Manager and the console/API), and to medium to see it as a single platform alongside its external dependencies."],[2292,"Symptom"],[1243,"Symptom or message"],[498,"Table (`table_name`)"],[2974,"Take a verifiable backup of PostgreSQL and of the CRL object storage — the VA bucket, or the local volume that holds the CRLs — and schedule downtime. The upgrade moves every service's data into `pki`, and the VA migration is irreversible: returning to 3.8.0 needs both backups (see CRL settings keyed by CA ID)."],[41,"Teams that want to use the platform without operating it"],[58,"Technical support and SLA according to your plan."],[939,"Test an allowed certificate, an incorrect one, another CN, webhook denial, timeout and re-enrollment under its own policy. Keep results and schedule bootstrap credential retirement where appropriate. Continue with EST client."],[1326,"Test an old identity allowed during overlap, a new one, an unknown chain and the result after removing old trust. Keep trust-store version, approved set, date and result. Reachable `/cacerts` e