acy references retained by the upgrade migration are described in the upgrade guide."],[2345,"The KMS unifies key lifecycle management and prevents every service from having to integrate directly with a specific cryptographic provider."],[96,"The Kubernetes cluster, nodes and persistent storage"],[290,"The Lamassu chart creates one shared Gateway with HTTP and HTTPS listeners. Envoy Gateway normally creates a dedicated proxy deployment and a `LoadBalancer` Service for it."],[371,"The Lamassu chart is an **application chart**, not a cluster bootstrap chart. It creates the Kubernetes resources that run and configure Lamassu, but it expects the platform services those resources depend on to exist."],[373,"The Lamassu chart provides"],[2314,"The list was fetched through a legacy `/crl/<ski>` URL and belongs to the CA that owned that SKI when the upgrade ran."],[2364,"The main KMS screen shows the complete inventory of keys registered in the system. It is the reference view for reviewing which keys exist, where they are kept and which entities they relate to."],[842,"The mental model of trust, keys, certificates and devices."],[731,"The Microsoft Teams and Webhook channels accept an optional `http_client` block that authenticates the call to the receiver. `auth_mode` selects `noauth` (the default), `apikey`, `jwt` or `mtls`; each mode requires its own options:"],[601,"The middleware extracts the credential and resolves the matching principals."],[794,"The middlewares publish the record after executing the operation, whether it succeeded or returned an error. This lets you investigate attempts as well as confirmed changes."],[2959,"The migration aborts, and the upgrade fails, on five kinds of data:"],[2958,"The migration that turns VA roles into CRL settings cannot be rolled back: its rollback does nothing. CRLs generated after the upgrade are stored under the CA ID, where 3.8.0 does not look for them, and the archived settings of CAs deleted before the upgrade have no si